# Your filled-in configuration — registry token, database URIs, JWT secret, provider keys.
# This repository is PUBLIC. Never commit it, and never commit a copy of it under another name:
# a timestamped backup is the usual way one gets published by accident.
.env
.env.*
# `.env.*` does NOT match `.production.env` — the name does not start with `.env.`. Without this
# line the production file, which holds every credential the deployment has, is untracked rather
# than ignored, and one `git add -A` publishes it on a public repository.
*.env
# Negations last, so the templates — which contain no values — stay tracked.
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# Created at runtime by the stack.
logs/
temp/
# The one real profile that is tracked: it names NO provider and holds no secret, and every
# deployment has to be able to select it (FALLBACK_PROFILE=none).
!llm/fallback-none.env
